 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A very severe cyclone just hit India's east coast. How bad was it?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "India's weather department says Cyclone Arnab, a very severe cyclonic storm born over the Bay of Bengal, crossed the Andhra Pradesh coast early Wednesday, near Narsapur. Winds were one hundred twenty-five to one hundred thirty-five kilometers an hour, with gusts up to one hundred fifty."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Reports say more than fifty thousand people were moved to shelters before the storm arrived. India's disaster response force confirms three deaths and thirty-one damaged houses. State radio reports extremely heavy rain at one hundred sixty-one locations."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "The chief minister's office says crops on seventy thousand nine hundred hectares were hit. Arnab has since weakened to a severe cyclonic storm. Early figures differ between reports, and officials are still counting. Heavy rain is expected in Odisha on Friday, reports say."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Odisha avoid the worst of the rain? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
